From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Mon, 27 Apr 2026 12:19:33 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: mtk_eth_soc: gate page_pool on XDP attachment

mtk_page_pool_enabled() reduces to mtk_is_netsys_v2_or_greater(), so on
MT7988 every RX ring is created with a page_pool and the hot path in
mtk_poll_rx() runs through the XDP/page_pool branch even with no XDP
program attached. That branch costs an RCU dereference of eth->prog per
packet, xdp_buff init/prepare, page_pool bookkeeping, and a PAGE_SIZE
SKB truesize, which caps forwarding well below line rate on this
dma-coherent SoC.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c |    2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/mediatek/mtk_eth_soc.c
@@ -3138,7 +3138,7 @@ static int mtk_rx_alloc(struct mtk_eth *
 	if (!ring->data)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth)) {
+	if (mtk_page_pool_enabled(eth) && rcu_access_pointer(eth->prog)) {
 		struct page_pool *pp;
 
 		pp = mtk_create_page_pool(eth, &ring->xdp_q, ring_no,
